The data files in this folder are third-party data from renewables.ninja
(https://www.renewables.ninja), hourly wind and solar PV capacity factors for
Jülich, Germany, for the year 2019. They are redistributed unmodified under the
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License
(CC BY-NC 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/). They are NOT
covered by the MIT License of the rest of this repository.

If you use these data, please cite:

S. Pfenninger and I. Staffell (2016). Long-term patterns of European PV output
using 30 years of validated hourly reanalysis and satellite data.
Energy 114, 1251-1265. doi:10.1016/j.energy.2016.08.060

I. Staffell and S. Pfenninger (2016). Using bias-corrected reanalysis to
simulate current and future wind power output.
Energy 114, 1224-1239. doi:10.1016/j.energy.2016.08.068
